Why Power BI?

Microsoft Power BI was selected because it provides tools for creating interactive and visually appealing dashboards.
Some important capabilities used in this project include:
- Interactive visualizations
- KPI cards
- Tables
- Slicers
- Filtering
- Data analysis
- Dashboard design
- Dynamic interaction between visuals
These features make it possible to present complex sales information in a form that is easier for users to understand.

Dashboard Design

The dashboard was designed to present the most important information first.
The KPI cards provide an immediate overview of business performance.
The charts provide visual comparisons and trends.
The customer table provides detailed information.
The slicers allow users to interact with the dashboard and investigate specific parts of the data.
This creates a logical flow from:
Summary → Trends → Comparisons → Detailed Analysis

